  "summary": "On 16 June 1963 Soviet cosmonaut Valentina Tereshkova was launched aboard Vostok 6, becoming the first woman to fly in space. She spent just under three days in orbit and landed on 19 June, parachuting to the ground in Kazakhstan northeast of Karaganda.",
